SOS2 port of Mesa 26.2.0 (tools/build_native_mesa.py): a POSIX-like host
system named 'sos2' with static EGL, GLES and Gallium archives, no regex,
sockets, SA_SIGINFO or per-thread CPU clocks, and a 32-bit off_t. Futexes map
to the SDK's sos2_wait/sos2_wake, so Mesa's many small locks never take one
of the SDK's fixed pthread mutex slots. Like other systems with libdrm, SOS2
asks the render node for PRIME support, which its libdrm shim provides for
EGL's dma-buf export.

